language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Assign people to tasks with different costs, so that the total cost is minimised.
given cost_dim1, cost_dim2 : int
given cost : matrix indexed by [int(1..cost_dim1), int(1..cost_dim2)] of int
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..cost_dim1), int(1..cost_dim2)] of bool
find total : int(0..1000000)

branching on [x]

minimising total
such that
$ each task must be assigned to exactly one person
forAll i : int(1..cost_dim1) . (sum j : int(1..cost_dim2) . x[i,j]) = 1,
$ it is not necessary to assign all people, but each person takes at most one task
forAll j : int(1..cost_dim2) . (sum i : int(1..cost_dim1) . x[i,j]) <= 1,
$ the total cost is the summed cost of the chosen assignments
total = (sum i : int(1..cost_dim1) . (sum j : int(1..cost_dim2) . cost[i,j] * x[i,j]))
